Sval: report the screen as a common resolution at or above the real one

Two RFPTargets, ScreenSizeCommon and ScreenSizeTight, make
screen.width/height and the CSS device-width/device-height media features
report the smallest common desktop resolution that is at least the real
screen in both dimensions, and derive ScreenAvailToResolution's available
screen from that size, so the screen, available screen and device size
always agree and the window never looks larger than the screen.
RFPTarget::ScreenRect reports the viewport instead, which makes screen equal
the window, a known tell. ScreenSizeTight, the strict control, picks from
four common 16:9 sizes (1366x768, 1920x1080, 2560x1440, 3840x2160), so many
more screens report the same size; it works with or without ScreenSizeCommon
and wins over it. Both targets are Doc-gated, so granularOverrides lifts
them per site.

The lists are SvalRFPService::GetSpoofedScreenSize, and the three sites ask
SvalRFPService::SpoofedScreenSize, so they cannot disagree. Sources:
StatCounter desktop screen resolution statistics
(gs.statcounter.com/screen-resolution-stats/desktop/worldwide, September
2026), the Steam Hardware Survey (September 2026), Apple's default scaled
sizes for current Macs (MacBook Air 13 and 15, MacBook Pro 14 and 16, iMac 24,
5K 27-inch), and 1920x1080 and 2560x1440 at Windows' 125% and 150% scaling. A
screen larger than every entry is rounded up to letterboxing's 200x100 steps,
or 1280x720 steps when tight.

No chrome API can change what nsScreen and nsMediaFeatures report.

diff --git a/dom/base/nsScreen.cpp b/dom/base/nsScreen.cpp
index 3b48a7f1e2..f9aeb73081 100644
--- a/dom/base/nsScreen.cpp
+++ b/dom/base/nsScreen.cpp
@@ -96,7 +96,14 @@ CSSIntRect nsScreen::GetRect() {
   if (NS_WARN_IF(!context)) {
     return {};
   }
-  return CSSIntRect::FromAppUnitsRounded(context->GetRect());
+  CSSIntRect rect = CSSIntRect::FromAppUnitsRounded(context->GetRect());
+  if (auto size = SvalRFPService::SpoofedScreenSize(
+          rect.Size(), [this](RFPTarget aTarget) {
+            return ShouldResistFingerprinting(aTarget);
+          })) {
+    return {{}, *size};
+  }
+  return rect;
 }
 
 CSSIntRect nsScreen::GetAvailRect() {
@@ -141,8 +148,18 @@ CSSIntRect nsScreen::GetAvailRect() {
       }
     }
 
+    // The available screen is derived from the screen this reports, so the
+    // two always agree.
+    nsRect screenRect = context->GetRect();
+    if (auto size = SvalRFPService::SpoofedScreenSize(
+            CSSIntRect::FromAppUnitsRounded(screenRect).Size(),
+            [this](RFPTarget aTarget) {
+              return ShouldResistFingerprinting(aTarget);
+            })) {
+      screenRect = CSSPixel::ToAppUnits(CSSIntRect({}, *size));
+    }
     return nsRFPService::GetSpoofedScreenAvailSize(
-        context->GetRect(), context->GetFullZoom(), IsFullscreen());
+        screenRect, context->GetFullZoom(), IsFullscreen());
   }
 
   nsDeviceContext* context = GetDeviceContext();
diff --git a/layout/style/nsMediaFeatures.cpp b/layout/style/nsMediaFeatures.cpp
index 1f9613b8cd..a39d07cc57 100644
--- a/layout/style/nsMediaFeatures.cpp
+++ b/layout/style/nsMediaFeatures.cpp
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "nsIPrintSettings.h"
 #include "nsIWidget.h"
 #include "nsPresContext.h"
+#include "nsRFPService.h"
 #include "nsStyleConsts.h"
 
 using namespace mozilla;
@@ -94,7 +95,15 @@ static nsSize GetDeviceSize(const Document& aDocument) {
     return pc->GetPageSize();
   }
 
-  return pc->DeviceContext()->GetDeviceSurfaceDimensions();
+  nsSize size = pc->DeviceContext()->GetDeviceSurfaceDimensions();
+  // The same size nsScreen::GetRect reports.
+  if (auto spoofed = SvalRFPService::SpoofedScreenSize(
